"Auto-bees" avoiding collisions
This year in order to drive the development of accident prevention technologies, this year Nissan was inspired by nature, more precarily from bees.
The Japanese company has developed a robot whose flight comes based upon bee spherical behavior, avoiding accidents.
This chemistry is a bio-mimetic car robot drive or BR23C and represents a first step in accident prevention technologies.
The engineer engineers from the technical development center of the Nissan Motor Co. have developed this small robot in cooperation with the Research Center for Advanced Science and Technology from the renowned university in Tokyo (Japan).
According to Kazuhiro Doi head technology PR and R&D-Brand-Management, the BR23C represents an extension of the four-pous Nissan safety shield.
This robot is designed to ensure that this brand’s vehicles are capable of avoiding collision.
During flight each bee establishes its own oval-shaped flight space, very similar to the Nissan safety shield.
But the most important pieces are the face-to-eyes of the bee, which can be seen over an angle of 300 degrees in all directions, which enables them to fly undisturbed in their personal spatial without interruption.
To replicate an e-around perspective, the technicians developed the so-called Laser Range Finder (LRF).
It notifies obstacles located at a distance up to two meters before BR23C up to two meters with a radius of 180 degrees calculates the distance to the object and sends a signal to an on-board microprocessor, which is immediately translated into signals to avoid the collision
"At the occasion when an obstacle is noticed, the small robot will imitate bee flight and immediately switch the direction by rotating his wheels at 90o or even greater nrails to avoid the collision.
The biggest distinction to any number of other systems is that this evasive manoeuvre occurs absolutely instinctive.
When it weren't, the robot might not be capable of reacting with adequate speed to avoid obstacles, said Toshiyuki Andoh, who explains principality for mobility laboratory and the senior engineer this project.
Uncorresponding to a bee, the robot may neither deviate upwards or down, but cannot excecances; it can only move on two dimensions and in the direction that enables him to rotate its wheels rather than infinite directions and infinite way, as the bees make.
For this reason, in addition to acceleration and deceleration function, Nissan has used the rotational function to avoid collision.
This device requires only each couple of seconds to include the information and act according to this information.
It requires neither to save the information nor the intuitive logic of manoeuvring taken, therefore it continuously means still a couple of small storage facilities.
That sounds surprising, but it'sn’t about the GB and not even talking about the storage space.
This is the first step in the development of technologies for immediate prevention collisions to introduce a technological enabling Nissan to introduce over the next ten years at serial vehicles.
The robot operates with lithium polymer batteries, which are easier and last longer than variety of lithium-ion battery.
Another possible application of this technology in the future could include integrating the unit using a GPS panoramic navigation system through satellite to lead to the destination while driving, avoiding obstacles along the way.
